{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install TanStack Charts and its React peers:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/charts react react-dom\npnpm add -D @types/react @types/react-dom","lang":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The shared "},{"type":"link","href":"../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scales"}]},{"type":"text","value":" page explains the\ncompact scale families and when a chart needs D3 instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"define-a-chart","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Define a chart"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definitions are ordinary framework-independent TypeScript:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"live-example","tagName":"md-live-example","attributes":{"id":"react-quick-start-1"},"properties":{"data-example-group":"react-quick-start","data-collapsed-indexes":"[1]","data-workspace":"{\"version\":1,\"entry\":\"/src/App.tsx\",\"environment\":\"charts-react\",\"files\":{\"/src/App.tsx\":\"import { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\\nimport { barY, defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\\nimport { alphabet } from './data'\\n\\nconst percent = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {\\n  style: 'percent',\\n  maximumFractionDigits: 1,\\n})\\n\\nconst letterFrequencyChart = defineChart({\\n  marks: [\\n    barY(alphabet, {\\n      x: 'letter',\\n      y: 'frequency',\\n    }),\\n  ],\\n  scales: {\\n    x: {\\n      scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\\n    },\\n    y: {\\n      scale: scaleLinear,\\n      nice: true,\\n      grid: true,\\n      axis: {\\n        label: 'Frequency',\\n        ticks: { format: (value) => percent.format(value) },\\n      },\\n    },\\n  },\\n\\n  tooltip,\\n})\\n\\nexport default function App() {\\n  return (\\n    <Chart\\n      definition={letterFrequencyChart}\\n      height={320}\\n      ariaLabel=\\\"English letter frequencies\\\"\\n    />\\n  )\\n}\",\"/src/data.ts\":\"export interface AlphabetRow {\\n  letter: string\\n  frequency: number\\n}\\n\\nexport const alphabet: readonly AlphabetRow[] = [\\n  { letter: 'E', frequency: 0.12702 },\\n  { letter: 'T', frequency: 0.09056 },\\n  { letter: 'A', frequency: 0.08167 },\\n  { letter: 'O', frequency: 0.07507 },\\n  { letter: 'I', frequency: 0.06966 },\\n]\"}}"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { barY, defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\nimport { alphabet } from './data'\n\nconst percent = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {\n  style: 'percent',\n  maximumFractionDigits: 1,\n})\n\nconst letterFrequencyChart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    barY(alphabet, {\n      x: 'letter',\n      y: 'frequency',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\n    },\n    y: {\n      scale: scaleLinear,\n      nice: true,\n      grid: true,\n      axis: {\n        label: 'Frequency',\n        ticks: { format: (value) => percent.format(value) },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n\n  tooltip,\n})\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n    />\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=react-quick-start env=charts-react file=/src/App.tsx entry","title":"/src/App.tsx","file":"/src/App.tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"export interface AlphabetRow {\n  letter: string\n  frequency: number\n}\n\nexport const alphabet: readonly AlphabetRow[] = [\n  { letter: 'E', frequency: 0.12702 },\n  { letter: 'T', frequency: 0.09056 },\n  { letter: 'A', frequency: 0.08167 },\n  { letter: 'O', frequency: 0.07507 },\n  { letter: 'I', frequency: 0.06966 },\n]","lang":"ts","meta":"group=react-quick-start file=/src/data.ts collapsed","title":"/src/data.ts","file":"/src/data.ts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The definition infers the original row and semantic x/y types. Do not add\ncomponent generics or cast the definition."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"responsive-sizing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive sizing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a fixed height with responsive width:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Or give the host a proportional box:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  aspectRatio={16 / 9}\n  initialWidth={720}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The outer element fills its available width when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" is absent. The\nadapter server-renders with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":", then the shared DOM host measures\nthe actual container after hydration. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./adapter.md#sizing-and-layout","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"memoize-live-definitions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memoize live definitions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a chart captures component values, memoize the complete definition:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useMemo } from 'react'\n\ninterface LetterFrequencyInput {\n  rows: readonly AlphabetRow[]\n  accent: string\n}\n\nexport function LiveLetterFrequency({ rows, accent }: LetterFrequencyInput) {\n  const definition = useMemo(() => {\n    return defineChart({\n      marks: [\n        barY(rows, {\n          x: 'letter',\n          y: 'frequency',\n          fill: accent,\n        }),\n      ],\n      scales: {\n        x: {\n          scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\n        },\n        y: {\n          scale: scaleLinear,\n          nice: true,\n        },\n      },\n\n      svgAnimation: true,\n      tooltip,\n    })\n  }, [rows, accent])\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={definition}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"Filtered English letter frequencies\"\n    />\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The application controls definition updates through the dependency list. A new\ndefinition identity tells TanStack Charts to rebuild the scene. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/chart-definitions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chart Definition API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"interaction-callbacks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interaction callbacks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callback types flow from the marks:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n  onFocusChange={(point) => {\n    if (point) {\n      console.log(point.datum.letter, point.yValue)\n    }\n  }}\n  onSelect={(point) => {\n    if (point) openLetter(point.datum.letter)\n  }}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The built-in tooltip is optional. Grouped focus, formatting, keyboard behavior,\nand application-owned interaction are documented in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/focus-and-interaction.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus and interaction"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"render-react-tooltip-content","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render React tooltip content"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react"},{"type":"text","value":" when the built-in tooltip is enough.\nTo pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderTooltipBody"},{"type":"text","value":", switch the component import to the optional React\ntooltip entry:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip'\n\nexport function ChartWithCustomTooltip() {\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n      renderTooltipBody={({ defaultBody, pinned, dismiss }) => (\n        <>\n          {defaultBody}\n          {pinned ? <button onClick={dismiss}>Close</button> : null}\n        </>\n      )}\n    />\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Existing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderTooltipBody"},{"type":"text","value":" users should migrate the component import from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip"},{"type":"text","value":". The definition\nstill uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/tooltip"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Continue with the "},{"type":"link","href":"./adapter.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for lifecycle and SSR, the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./reference/chart.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for every prop, or the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/index.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"core API reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for definitions, marks, scales,\nand rendering."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"define-a-chart","text":"Define a chart","level":2},{"id":"responsive-sizing","text":"Responsive sizing","level":2},{"id":"memoize-live-definitions","text":"Memoize live definitions","level":2},{"id":"interaction-callbacks","text":"Interaction callbacks","level":2},{"id":"render-react-tooltip-content","text":"Render React tooltip content","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nInstall TanStack Charts and its React peers:\n\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts react react-dom\npnpm add -D @types/react @types/react-dom\n```\n\nThe shared [Scales](../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md) page explains the\ncompact scale families and when a chart needs D3 instead.\n\n## Define a chart\n\nDefinitions are ordinary framework-independent TypeScript:\n\n```tsx group=react-quick-start env=charts-react file=/src/App.tsx entry\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { barY, defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\nimport { alphabet } from './data'\n\nconst percent = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {\n  style: 'percent',\n  maximumFractionDigits: 1,\n})\n\nconst letterFrequencyChart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    barY(alphabet, {\n      x: 'letter',\n      y: 'frequency',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\n    },\n    y: {\n      scale: scaleLinear,\n      nice: true,\n      grid: true,\n      axis: {\n        label: 'Frequency',\n        ticks: { format: (value) => percent.format(value) },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n\n  tooltip,\n})\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```ts group=react-quick-start file=/src/data.ts collapsed\nexport interface AlphabetRow {\n  letter: string\n  frequency: number\n}\n\nexport const alphabet: readonly AlphabetRow[] = [\n  { letter: 'E', frequency: 0.12702 },\n  { letter: 'T', frequency: 0.09056 },\n  { letter: 'A', frequency: 0.08167 },\n  { letter: 'O', frequency: 0.07507 },\n  { letter: 'I', frequency: 0.06966 },\n]\n```\n\nThe definition infers the original row and semantic x/y types. Do not add\ncomponent generics or cast the definition.\n\n## Responsive sizing\n\nUse a fixed height with responsive width:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n/>\n```\n\nOr give the host a proportional box:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  aspectRatio={16 / 9}\n  initialWidth={720}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n/>\n```\n\nThe outer element fills its available width when `width` is absent. The\nadapter server-renders with `initialWidth`, then the shared DOM host measures\nthe actual container after hydration. See\n[React adapter](./adapter.md#sizing-and-layout).\n\n## Memoize live definitions\n\nWhen a chart captures component values, memoize the complete definition:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useMemo } from 'react'\n\ninterface LetterFrequencyInput {\n  rows: readonly AlphabetRow[]\n  accent: string\n}\n\nexport function LiveLetterFrequency({ rows, accent }: LetterFrequencyInput) {\n  const definition = useMemo(() => {\n    return defineChart({\n      marks: [\n        barY(rows, {\n          x: 'letter',\n          y: 'frequency',\n          fill: accent,\n        }),\n      ],\n      scales: {\n        x: {\n          scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\n        },\n        y: {\n          scale: scaleLinear,\n          nice: true,\n        },\n      },\n\n      svgAnimation: true,\n      tooltip,\n    })\n  }, [rows, accent])\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={definition}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"Filtered English letter frequencies\"\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe application controls definition updates through the dependency list. A new\ndefinition identity tells TanStack Charts to rebuild the scene. See\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n\n## Interaction callbacks\n\nCallback types flow from the marks:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n  onFocusChange={(point) => {\n    if (point) {\n      console.log(point.datum.letter, point.yValue)\n    }\n  }}\n  onSelect={(point) => {\n    if (point) openLetter(point.datum.letter)\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\nThe built-in tooltip is optional. Grouped focus, formatting, keyboard behavior,\nand application-owned interaction are documented in\n[Focus and interaction](../../reference/focus-and-interaction.md).\n\n## Render React tooltip content\n\nKeep `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/react` when the built-in tooltip is enough.\nTo pass `renderTooltipBody`, switch the component import to the optional React\ntooltip entry:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip'\n\nexport function ChartWithCustomTooltip() {\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n      renderTooltipBody={({ defaultBody, pinned, dismiss }) => (\n        <>\n          {defaultBody}\n          {pinned ? <button onClick={dismiss}>Close</button> : null}\n        </>\n      )}\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\nExisting `renderTooltipBody` users should migrate the component import from\n`@tanstack/charts/react` to `@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip`. The definition\nstill uses `tooltip` from `@tanstack/charts/tooltip`.\n\nContinue with the [React adapter](./adapter.md) for lifecycle and SSR, the\n[`Chart` reference](./reference/chart.md) for every prop, or the\n[core API reference](../../reference/index.md) for definitions, marks, scales,\nand rendering.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: React Quick Start\ndescription: Install the React adapter, define a typed chart, render responsive SVG, and add native interaction.\n---\n\nInstall TanStack Charts and its React peers:\n\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts react react-dom\npnpm add -D @types/react @types/react-dom\n```\n\nThe shared [Scales](../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md) page explains the\ncompact scale families and when a chart needs D3 instead.\n\n## Define a chart\n\nDefinitions are ordinary framework-independent TypeScript:\n\n```tsx group=react-quick-start env=charts-react file=/src/App.tsx entry\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { barY, defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\nimport { alphabet } from './data'\n\nconst percent = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {\n  style: 'percent',\n  maximumFractionDigits: 1,\n})\n\nconst letterFrequencyChart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    barY(alphabet, {\n      x: 'letter',\n      y: 'frequency',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\n    },\n    y: {\n      scale: scaleLinear,\n      nice: true,\n      grid: true,\n      axis: {\n        label: 'Frequency',\n        ticks: { format: (value) => percent.format(value) },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n\n  tooltip,\n})\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```ts group=react-quick-start file=/src/data.ts collapsed\nexport interface AlphabetRow {\n  letter: string\n  frequency: number\n}\n\nexport const alphabet: readonly AlphabetRow[] = [\n  { letter: 'E', frequency: 0.12702 },\n  { letter: 'T', frequency: 0.09056 },\n  { letter: 'A', frequency: 0.08167 },\n  { letter: 'O', frequency: 0.07507 },\n  { letter: 'I', frequency: 0.06966 },\n]\n```\n\nThe definition infers the original row and semantic x/y types. Do not add\ncomponent generics or cast the definition.\n\n## Responsive sizing\n\nUse a fixed height with responsive width:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n/>\n```\n\nOr give the host a proportional box:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  aspectRatio={16 / 9}\n  initialWidth={720}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n/>\n```\n\nThe outer element fills its available width when `width` is absent. The\nadapter server-renders with `initialWidth`, then the shared DOM host measures\nthe actual container after hydration. See\n[React adapter](./adapter.md#sizing-and-layout).\n\n## Memoize live definitions\n\nWhen a chart captures component values, memoize the complete definition:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useMemo } from 'react'\n\ninterface LetterFrequencyInput {\n  rows: readonly AlphabetRow[]\n  accent: string\n}\n\nexport function LiveLetterFrequency({ rows, accent }: LetterFrequencyInput) {\n  const definition = useMemo(() => {\n    return defineChart({\n      marks: [\n        barY(rows, {\n          x: 'letter',\n          y: 'frequency',\n          fill: accent,\n        }),\n      ],\n      scales: {\n        x: {\n          scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\n        },\n        y: {\n          scale: scaleLinear,\n          nice: true,\n        },\n      },\n\n      svgAnimation: true,\n      tooltip,\n    })\n  }, [rows, accent])\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={definition}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"Filtered English letter frequencies\"\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe application controls definition updates through the dependency list. A new\ndefinition identity tells TanStack Charts to rebuild the scene. See\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n\n## Interaction callbacks\n\nCallback types flow from the marks:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n  onFocusChange={(point) => {\n    if (point) {\n      console.log(point.datum.letter, point.yValue)\n    }\n  }}\n  onSelect={(point) => {\n    if (point) openLetter(point.datum.letter)\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\nThe built-in tooltip is optional. Grouped focus, formatting, keyboard behavior,\nand application-owned interaction are documented in\n[Focus and interaction](../../reference/focus-and-interaction.md).\n\n## Render React tooltip content\n\nKeep `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/react` when the built-in tooltip is enough.\nTo pass `renderTooltipBody`, switch the component import to the optional React\ntooltip entry:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip'\n\nexport function ChartWithCustomTooltip() {\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n      renderTooltipBody={({ defaultBody, pinned, dismiss }) => (\n        <>\n          {defaultBody}\n          {pinned ? <button onClick={dismiss}>Close</button> : null}\n        </>\n      )}\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\nExisting `renderTooltipBody` users should migrate the component import from\n`@tanstack/charts/react` to `@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip`. The definition\nstill uses `tooltip` from `@tanstack/charts/tooltip`.\n\nContinue with the [React adapter](./adapter.md) for lifecycle and SSR, the\n[`Chart` reference](./reference/chart.md) for every prop, or the\n[core API reference](../../reference/index.md) for definitions, marks, scales,\nand rendering.\n"}
